Assert unwind safety of the callbacks handed to the browser

When panics unwind, wasm-bindgen catches a panic in a closure handed to
JavaScript and turns it into a JavaScript exception, but only for a closure
whose captures are unwind safe. The dispatcher's main-thread tasks, the DOM
event listeners and the window's observers capture boxed callbacks or the
window's shared state, which are not, so the crate fails to compile.
Asserting it gives them the handling every other closure of the crate has.

